{
    "_doc": "Arms and armour (systems/arms.js). Every weapon, shield, helm and body armour the player can forge, buy, wear, wield and issue to troops. An item's stats: slot (main | off | head | body), class (dagger, sword, axe, mace, spear, polearm, bow, crossbow, shield, helm, padded, leather, mail, plate), material (bronze, iron, steel, wood, leather, cloth), hands (2 = no shield), cut / pierce / blunt (0-10: the duel's weapon damage is the best of the three / 2, its damage type the best of the three), reach (0-3: the longer weapon hits more often on strike and thrust), weight (kg: heavy weapons cost breath to swing, heavy harness costs stamina), attack (handling: added to the duel's attack), pen (0-1: the share of the defender's armour the blow ignores — maces and points go through mail), edge (true: the blade dulls and wants sharpening), wear (how fast it wears: 1 = normal), tier (what it is worth on a soldier: bronze 0.85, iron 1, steel 1.15), block / riposte (shields: duel guard and riposte), cover (shields: share of a missile or ambush blow it takes), prot (armour: share of each blow it stops) with vs (how well it stops cut / pierce / blunt), melee (false: a bow is no duelling weapon), repair (what mending it takes), sprite (for the renderers: weaponClass and the LPC layers under assets/lpc/Characters: layer, the piece in front of the body; behind, its frames where it passes behind the body; layers, the piece's composited layers bottom to top when there are several; paint, a shield's livery paint (a folder of colours). Body armour names the masculine build's sheets, the feminine build's sit at the same path under Clothing/Feminine, Thin. The art: scripts/make_arms_layers.py, make_arms_shields.py, make_arms_wear.py). Grades (core/grades.js) scale damage, block, cover and prot by their effect multiplier. troops: what each soldier must be issued (systems/arms.js issueKit) — per unit type, the slots with their weight in his worth and the classes that fill them; bare is what an unarmed man is worth against a fully armed one.",
