    "realms": {
        "_doc": "The crowns' armouries (world/realmArms.js, kingdom.armoury). A realm's army (kingdom.military, in men) needs a kit per menPerKit men: a weapon (main) for its foot and horse, a bow (ranged) for its archers (its composition's archer share), a shield (off) for the foot, a helm and a body armour for every man, and quiver arrows per archer kit. Every buyEvery days the crown buys what it lacks out of its own towns' market stock (at most marketShare of a town's stock at a time, the cheapest good of the slot first, at the town's price, paid from the treasury into the town's purse, booked as the army's arms line), spending at most spendShare of what the treasury holds above its reserve (reserveBase + reservePerMan x men). Pieces wear out: wear.peace of them a day, wear.war at war (this is the realm's draw on the towns' arms: the old warMult stand-in is gone). A battle: each side loses the arms of its fallen (the men lost x lostShare of the pieces); the side holding the field recovers recoverOwn of its own and strips strip of the beaten's; each side looses perBattle arrows per archer kit (the victor picks up arrowRecover of its own). A host sent against the player (systems/realmWars.js) takes its share of the armoury with it, brings back what survives, and loses it all when broken. More than keep x the need in store (after a demobilisation, a rich haul) is sold back to the realm's best-stocked market at sellShare of its price, as far as the town's purse pays. Battle power x the army's arms factor: (1 - archers) x the soldier's kit worth + archers x the archer's (troops.kits soldier/archer weights; a filled slot = its fill x the pieces' average tier; a bow without arrows at dryMult), clamped to [minFactor, troops.maxFactor]. A new realm starts with start of its need in its arsenals.",
